Since \(Y_i = f(\mathbf{x}_i, \theta) + \epsilon_i\), \(\epsilon_i \sim \text{iid}(0, \sigma^2)\), can estimate parameters (\(\hat{\theta}\)) minimizing sum squared errors:\[
