\]\(c\) controls strength prior. prior information available, can set \(c = 0\) \(P(\rho) \propto 1\).Example: Combining Estimates Two StudiesLet:Current study: \(r_{\text{likelihood}} = 0.5\), \(n_{\text{likelihood}} = 200\)Prior study: \(r_{\text{prior}} = 0.2765\), \(n_{\text{prior}} = 50205\)Step 1: Posterior Variance\[
